-- title:
--   Igusa ramification formula via equivariant torsion reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $N\ge 1$ an integer with $(N:K)\ne 0$, $j_0\in K$, and $E_0$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $K$. Let $M$ be a field extension of $K$ and $t\in M$ transcendental over $K$ with $M/K\langle t\rangle$ finite and Galois. Let $E$ denote the base change to $M$ of the Weierstrass curve `ofJ` of invariant $t$ over $K\langle t\rangle$, and let $W_0$ be a place of $M$ over $K$ (a proper valuation subring of $M$ containing $K$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring) with $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(t-j_0)>0$, where $\operatorname{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Assume given an additive map $\theta\colon E(M)\to E_0(K)$ and a map $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(M/K\langle t\rangle)$ to variable changes over $K$, subject to: $E(M)$ has exactly $N^2$ points killed by $N$; $\theta$ is injective on the $N$-torsion; for every $\sigma$ whose induced semilinear automorphism fixes $W_0$, $\rho(\sigma)\cdot E_0=E_0$ and $\mathrm{vcInvFun}(\rho(\sigma))$ applied to $\theta P$ equals $\theta(\sigma P)$ for all $P$ (as an equality of terms in possibly distinct types); and conversely every $\gamma$ with $\gamma\cdot E_0=E_0$ satisfies, for some such $\sigma$, $\mathrm{vcInvFun}(\gamma)(\theta P)=\pm\theta(\sigma P)$ for all $P$. Let $Q\in E(M)$ have exact additive order $N$, assume the Vélu full-kernel quotient $E/\langle Q\rangle$ (formed from the odd-order summing set of $Q$ up to $N-1$) has nonzero discriminant, and let $\psi$ be a $K$-algebra map from the subfield $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,K\,N$ of $K((q))$, generated over $K$ by the series $q$-expanded $j$'s $j(q^d)$ for $d\mid N$, into $M$ with $\psi(j(q))=t$ and $\psi(j(q^N))=j(E/\langle Q\rangle)$. Then $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(t-j_0)$ times the number of variable changes $\gamma$ over $K$ with $\gamma\cdot E_0=E_0$ carrying the subgroup of integer multiples of $\theta Q$ into itself equals the ramification index of $W_0$ along $\psi$ (the least positive $n$ of the form $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(\psi f)$ with $f\ne 0$) times the order of the stabiliser of $E_0$ in the group of variable changes over $K$, as an identity in $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is Igusa's description of the ramification of $X_0(N)\to X(1)$ above $j=j_0$, cast in a Galois frame: after dividing by the ramification index along $\psi$, it identifies the local degree with the index in $\operatorname{Aut}(E_0)$ of the stabiliser of the cyclic subgroup generated by $\theta Q$, i.e. with the number of cyclic subgroups of order $N$ in the $\operatorname{Aut}(E_0)$-orbit of $\langle\theta Q\rangle$. It is used by the two downstream ramification statements for places of the modular function field lying over $j=j_0$, which feed the analysis of the reduction of the $X_0(N)$ covering.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_mul_natCard_stabilizer_eq_ramificationIndexAlong_mul_of_equivariant_torsion_reduction.lean

